Why Is Demand Increasing
Automotive electronics: Rising electronic content and reliability requirements are increasing demand for robust surge and ESD protection.
High-speed interfaces: Lower-capacitance protection is becoming important for high-speed data interfaces.
Compact electronics: Compact SMD packaging is becoming a key competitive differentiator as system designers seek higher performance and lower system-level cost.
Fab & Technology Pulse

TVS diode technology is moving toward a combination of lower capacitance, higher surge robustness and smaller packages. Unidirectional TVS products remain a leading segment, reflecting their broad use across high-volume protection applications. At the technology level, surface-mount devices support compact electronic designs, while through-hole devices remain relevant in applications requiring particular mechanical or electrical characteristics. Automotive qualification is becoming increasingly important as vehicles incorporate more electronic control systems. Suppliers including Vishay, Littelfuse, onsemi and STMicroelectronics are developing portfolios covering automotive, industrial and communications applications.

